The `sortLayerEntries` function is not robust against non-array inputs or nullish elements. If `items` is not an array, `[...items]` will throw a TypeError. Additionally, if any element in `items` is null or undefined, accessing properties like `left.assertion_id` will throw a TypeError. Adding defensive guards and filtering out nullish elements ensures robustness.

```suggestion
function sortLayerEntries(items) {
  if (!Array.isArray(items)) return [];
  return [...items].filter((item) => item !== null && item !== undefined).sort((left, right) => (
    compareByteOrder(
      left?.assertion_id ?? left?.source_blocker_id ?? left?.promotion_assertion_id,
      right?.assertion_id ?? right?.source_blocker_id ?? right?.promotion_assertion_id
    ) ||
    compareByteOrder(left?.question_row_id, right?.question_row_id) ||
    compareByteOrder(left?.promotion_assertion_id, right?.promotion_assertion_id)
  ));
}
```

