The `buildLayers` function is not robust against non-array inputs or missing/malformed properties on `rows`. If `rows` is not an array, iterating over it will throw a TypeError. Similarly, if `row.classified_assertions` or `row.terminal_blocker_classifications` are missing or not arrays, it will throw a TypeError. Adding defensive guards ensures the function fails closed gracefully.

