The `buildSummary` function assumes `rows` is always a valid array. If `rows` is nullish or not an array, calling `rows.flatMap` will throw a TypeError. Adding defensive guards to default to an empty array ensures robustness.

```javascript
function buildSummary({ rows, layers, classification }) {
  const safeRows = Array.isArray(rows) ? rows : [];
  const assertions = safeRows.flatMap((row) => row?.classified_assertions ?? []);
  const blockers = safeRows.flatMap((row) => row?.terminal_blocker_classifications ?? []);
```

