The `isSortedById` function is not robust against non-array inputs or nullish elements. If `items` is not an array, calling `items.map` will throw a TypeError. Additionally, if any element in `items` is null or undefined, accessing properties like `item.assertion_id` will throw a TypeError. Adding defensive guards ensures robustness.

```suggestion
function isSortedById(items) {
  if (!Array.isArray(items)) return true;
  const ids = items.map((item) => (
    item?.assertion_id ?? item?.source_blocker_id ?? item?.promotion_assertion_id
  ));
  return sameList(ids, [...ids].sort(compareByteOrder));
}
```

